{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "generation_contexts": [{"context_id": "sha256:3118c7dde979a421372b20a0468066cd51acb0c79815e5a0533b585003b513dc", "hash": "sha256:3118c7dde979a421372b20a0468066cd51acb0c79815e5a0533b585003b513dc", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 29301, "byte_start": 29111, "file": "properties.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:d8cdea42ba22b0c8097584385b4fff3d96fbb91484d3b0d3b202d865e7ab147a", "line_end": 815, "line_start": 812}, "owner_tag": "01P1", "parent_tag": "01P1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-ubiquity-Jacobson-schemes}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c9632c85c98aefceea3881efdd73f0083e0fc0fbb8d9d0469711c08e97277fc6", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nMany schemes used commonly in algebraic geometry are Jacobson, see\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nWe mention here the following interesting case.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8be3b27e0d236aaaa9815d8b1ab7f6c1102ada29e3d16a1145378aa448fe3a25", "unit_id": "inventory:properties:01P1:paragraph/0004"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:4039ed98f410adcc409387af011fec1a963c5d02e7739786897ec9debe74fef5", "hash": "sha256:4039ed98f410adcc409387af011fec1a963c5d02e7739786897ec9debe74fef5", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 31127, "byte_start": 29915, "file": "properties.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:fd14075f551c6b9b965456a5aea4a6297bba11eeb33d030a2ded8db956c0c8b6", "line_end": 858, "line_start": 833}, "owner_tag": "02IM", "parent_tag": "01P1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01P1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(R) - V(I)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Spec(R_f)$", "MATH_0003": "$f \\in I$", "MATH_0004": "$R_f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Spec(R) \\setminus V(I)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$S$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$\\xi \\in S$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{\\xi\\}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathfrak p \\subset R$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathfrak q$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathfrak p \\subset \\mathfrak q \\subset \\mathfrak m$", "MATH_0015": "$\\{\\mathfrak p\\}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\Spec(R/\\mathfrak p)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-lemma-noetherian-zariski-jacobson-complement}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locally-jacobson}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-locally-closed-in-Noetherian}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-scheme-sober}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{topology-lemma-non-jacobson-Noetherian-characterize}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-Noetherian-local-domain-dim-2-infinite-opens}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b18823307aad84e5120c68c1e5d4220a7931c9f383d8f8024801d9b6b9ec31af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c659f3e72d2dbf249cfe823ebb3201b6bd19ba27af57dc3b79f8c27d8e0a3b27", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nProof of (3). Observe that <MATH_0001> has a covering by the affine\nopens <MATH_0002> for <MATH_0003>. The rings <MATH_0004> are Jacobson by\nMore on Algebra, Lemma\n<REF_0001>.\nHence <MATH_0005> is Jacobson by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nParts (1) and (2) are special cases of (3).\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nDirect proof of case (1).\nSince <MATH_0006> is a Noetherian scheme,\n<MATH_0007> is a Noetherian scheme (Lemma <REF_0003>).\nHence <MATH_0008> is a sober, Noetherian topological space (use\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0004>).\nAssume <MATH_0009> is not Jacobson to\nget a contradiction. By\nTopology, Lemma <REF_0005>\nthere exists some non-closed point <MATH_0010>\nsuch that <MATH_0011> is locally closed. This corresponds\nto a prime <MATH_0012> such that (1) there exists\na prime <MATH_0013>, <MATH_0014>\nwith both inclusions strict, and (2) <MATH_0015> is open in\n<MATH_0016>. This is impossible by Algebra,\nLemma <REF_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6db185ed736217ae49b69dffa4e5d791ebe13a38e29a06d24a902d775d091e68", "unit_id": "inventory:properties:02IM:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "sha256:df02f4cce3ad7372b91cf50c51082dd21abe7ee5db0a5915fea55809003f8124", "hash": "sha256:df02f4cce3ad7372b91cf50c51082dd21abe7ee5db0a5915fea55809003f8124", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 85603, "byte_start": 85437, "file": "more-algebra.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:f5c8587c0edced1356885bc364ce326b1f1b4b1acf3add3387ef1aa7f0a0765d", "line_end": 2249, "line_start": 2245}, "owner_tag": "0ELY", "parent_tag": "0ELX", "requested_label": "more-algebra-definition-zariski-pair", "requested_tag": "0ELY", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "more-algebra", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0ELX", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{definition-zariski-pair}", "MATH_0001": "$(A, I)$", "MATH_0002": "$I$", "MATH_0003": "$A$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{definition}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{definition}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d44c2f72b5847b21f85687b10801359b76c31e526da40d18195923c808e6d7aa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:063e5b6cfffbf3056d3a9a8072a07b397c260cc2